UwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2025-02-21T15:05:10Z","updated_at":"2025-02-21T15:05:10Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n4.4 beta4\n\n### System information\n\nW10\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen you have any Shader open in Shader Editor and save a scene, even if the shader is not modified, it can cause it to be saved. This is because the shader is incorrectly marked as \"edited\" when it's loaded in the editor:\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/394508d26dcf1b7a9362453f9009c07d969f1a7e/editor/plugins/text_shader_editor.cpp#L995\nAfter saving it once, the incorrect saving won't happen again for the editor session.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open a Shader in Shader Editor\n2. Save a scene (Ctrl+S)\n3. The shader is also saved\n\nBest tested with existing shader, because it's easier to track modified time.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103128/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/103128/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}